            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. A driveway is a large, trafficked, UV-exposed slab with moisture moving through it from below — the exact combination a rubberised patch coating handles worst. It will scuff under tyres, lift where vapour pushes from beneath, and cost several times more per square foot than a proper driveway sealer.",
