          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Flex Seal on concrete</strong> is a question of scale and exposure, not of adhesion. Small, contained, out of the way and out of the traffic: it works. Large, walked on, driven on or below grade: it fails, and it fails in a way that makes the eventual proper repair harder.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Before any impermeable coating goes onto a slab, tape down a square of plastic overnight and look for condensation underneath. That one test predicts more coating failures than any product review can, and it costs nothing but an evening of patience and a scrap of plastic sheet.
          </p>
